instruction:
You are tasked with creating a Verilog module that takes in two input signals, `a` and `b`, and produces two output signals, `sum` and `carry`. The module should implement a full adder logic and should use the following Verilog code snippet as a starting point:

```
module full_adder(a, b, sum, carry);
   input a, b;
   output sum, carry;
   // Your code here
endmodule
```

Your task is to complete the code snippet to implement the full adder logic.

original_rtl:
module full_adder(a, b, sum, carry);
   input a, b;
   output sum, carry;
   wire w1, w2, w3;
   assign w1 = a ^ b;
   assign w2 = a & b;
   assign w3 = w2 | (w1 & carry);
   assign sum = w1 ^ carry;
   assign carry = w3;
endmodule

